# <function> <scalar-pointer-arg> ...
# Every typed pointer not listed here is treated as a data buffer.
# workSize of the plan and size routines stays a scalar, which is right for a plan on
# one GPU. On a plan spread over several GPUs (hipfftXtSetGPUs), hipFFT writes one
# work size per GPU: such a caller passes c_loc of an array to the bind(C) form.
hipfftEstimate1d workSize
hipfftEstimate2d workSize
hipfftEstimate3d workSize
hipfftEstimateMany workSize
hipfftGetProperty value
hipfftGetSize workSize
hipfftGetSize1d workSize
hipfftGetSize2d workSize
hipfftGetSize3d workSize
hipfftGetSizeMany workSize
hipfftGetSizeMany64 workSize
hipfftGetVersion version
hipfftMakePlan1d workSize
hipfftMakePlan2d workSize
hipfftMakePlan3d workSize
hipfftMakePlanMany workSize
hipfftMakePlanMany64 workSize
hipfftXtGetSizeMany workSize
hipfftXtMakePlanMany workSize
